        "content": {
          "kind": "html",
          "value": "<div style='width:100%;height:100%;overflow:auto;box-sizing:border-box;container-type:inline-size;background:#ffffff;font-family:Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#0f172a'><div style='box-sizing:border-box;max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 clamp(20px,5cqw,40px) 64px'><div style='padding-top:32px'><header data-role='masthead'><div style='padding:10px 0;border-top:3px solid #0f172a;border-bottom:1px solid #0f172a;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>TWILITE ZONE · CONTRACT</div><h1 style='margin:40px 0 0;font:500 clamp(40px,9.5cqw,72px)/.98 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.025em;text-wrap:balance;color:#0f172a'>Twilite Structural Model Inventory</h1></header></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><div style='display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;flex-direction:row-reverse;align-items:flex-start;gap:32px 40px'><div style='flex:1 1 220px;min-width:0'><section data-role='settings' style='padding-top:10px;border-top:3px solid #0f172a'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#0f172a'>At a glance</h2><dl style='margin:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:max-content 1fr;column-gap:12px;border-bottom:1px solid #cbd5e1'><dt style='grid-column:1/-1;padding:9px 0 0px;border-top:1px solid #cbd5e1;font:400 13px/20px system-ui;color:#475569'>Status</dt><dd style='grid-column:1/-1;margin:0;padding:2px 0 9px;font:600 14px/20px system-ui;color:#0f172a;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>working inventory for current authoring. Settled rules are normative for new graphs. Items marked provisional are implementation targets, not law.</dd></dl></section></div><div style='flex:999 1 380px;min-width:0'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Identity and containment</h2><ul style='margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:22px;max-width:60ch;font:400 18px/1.55 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>A <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>.node</code> document is a graph: a bounded authored contribution with its own nodes, edges, settings, and save address.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>The <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>root</code> owns graph identity and intent. <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>data.identity.graphId</code> identifies the graph contribution; <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>data.identity.nodeId</code> identifies the semantic node that contribution represents when a node spans several graph documents.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>A workspace is a graph-level composition. It stores durable graph or exposed-Surface references plus arrangement and camera state; it does not copy every child graph into the workspace document.</li></ul></section></div></div></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Node rendering</h2><ul style='margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:22px;max-width:60ch;font:400 18px/1.55 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>Nodes render through ordered <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>face</code> nodes. Durable material belongs to <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>content</code>; a face may own <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>data.content</code> directly or point to a content node.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>The <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>root</code> is the implicit root Port. New graphs do not add a second root Port node.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>A <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>surface</code> edge starts each Surface chain. <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>next-face</code> edges order faces from richest to smallest, and the chain ends in a <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>glyph</code>.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>A graph may expose sparse faces. Missing smaller bands use the nearest authored face; do not create Detail, Summary, and Icon faces merely to fill bands.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>A <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>ground</code> edge anchors entry, focus, and authored interface geometry when the graph has an inside frame. A document graph may omit ground.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>Focus affects interaction and camera scope. It does not silently change semantic identity or rewrite the graph.</li></ul></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Ports, Portals, Bridges, and edges</h2><ul style='margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:22px;max-width:60ch;font:400 18px/1.55 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>A Port exposes a typed capability or named Surface at a node boundary. Handles are draggable UI representations of Ports; edges connect to semantic ports.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>A Portal consumes or follows an exposed Port and never creates an ordinary node merely because it was followed.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>An authored edge belongs to one graph document and connects nodes through explicit Port ids. Edge kind is stored in <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>type</code>; class graph in <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>data.classRef</code>.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>Export and import nodes are Bridge ends. A Bridge is the workspace connection and is not authored as a <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>bridge</code> node.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>Workspace navigation policy (<code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>navigate</code>, <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>expand</code>, <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>open alongside</code>) is independent of security classification.</li></ul></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Presentation geometry</h2><ul style='margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:22px;max-width:60ch;font:400 18px/1.55 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>Graph extent, the root-to-ground interface frame, Surface bounds, and internal graph camera are distinct values.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>Node <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>width</code> and <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>height</code> size the node shell in its owning graph.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>The authored root-to-ground frame is the graph-backed node&#39;s shape in a workspace. Its border, hit area, Minimap window, edge apertures, and semantic-zoom measurement share those bounds.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>An unfocused graph-backed node clips nodes and edges outside that frame. Authors enlarge or reshape the frame when that material must appear in the node or its Minimap representation.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>Workspace zoom scales the authored shape and uses its resulting screen occupancy to choose semantic representation.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>A focused graph unfolds the complete source graph. Camera rollover may then transfer control into graph-local scope; neither operation enlarges the authored workspace shape.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>The active graph&#39;s main minimap is a navigation instrument over the complete graph.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>A deliberate workspace resize is an arrangement-local viewport override. It does not move source nodes or change graph extent.</li></ul></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Remaining model gaps</h2><h3 style='margin:22px 0 8px;font:700 15px/20px system-ui;color:#0f172a'>P0 — Face fitting and camera rollover</h3><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>Define:</p><ul style='margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:22px;max-width:60ch;font:400 18px/1.55 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>whether a face uses responsive, contain, cover, or fixed-aspect fitting;</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>exact hysteresis and anchor rules when zoom crosses between workspace and graph-local camera scope.</li></ul><h3 style='margin:22px 0 8px;font:700 15px/20px system-ui;color:#0f172a'>P0 — Edge lanes</h3><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>Define lane identity, ownership, allocation, routing, editing, projection across graph/workspace seams, persistence, and interaction with manual route pins. See <a href='https://twilite.zone/library/documentation/contracts/edges/edge-lane-contract.md' style='color:#6d28d9;text-decoration:underline'>Edge Lane Contract</a>.</p><h3 style='margin:22px 0 8px;font:700 15px/20px system-ui;color:#0f172a'>P1 — Current-graph conformance and migration</h3><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>Create an executable profile that distinguishes valid current graphs, valid legacy graphs readable through compatibility, incomplete graphs missing required identity or presentation, and mechanical migrations from legacy inline Port presentation and duplicated root Ports.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Rewrite rule</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>Do not bulk-normalize graphs by shape alone. For each graph:</p><ol style='margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:26px;max-width:60ch;font:400 18px/1.55 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>preserve <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>graphId</code>, <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>nodeId</code>, durable address, and semantic type;</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>identify its root, Surfaces, faces, glyphs, exposed Ports, Portals, Bridges, and typed edges;</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>separate graph extent from presentation geometry;</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>migrate only rules marked settled above;</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>defer render-size and lane rewrites until their provisional contracts are ratified;</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'>validate save/reload, navigation, semantic zoom, and edge endpoint integrity.</li></ol></section></div><div style='padding-top:40px'><div style='display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:stretch;gap:28px 32px'><div style='flex:1 1 190px;min-width:0'><section data-role='route' data-prominence='secondary' style='height:100%;box-sizing:border-box;display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #0f172a'><h2 style='margin:0 0 8px;font:500 22px/1.1 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.01em;color:#0f172a'>Contracts</h2><p style='margin:0 0 10px;font:400 14px/1.55 system-ui;color:#475569'>The contracts that use the current vocabulary.</p><a data-role='route-link' href='tlz://twilite.zone/library/documentation/contracts/root.node' style='margin-top:auto;font:700 13px/20px system-ui;text-decoration:none;color:#475569'>Open the contracts →</a></section></div></div></div></div></div>"
        },
        "memo": "",
        "link": ""
      }
    },
