    {
      "id": "structural-model-section-4",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Presentation geometry",
      "position": {
        "x": 380,
        "y": -280
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 320,
      "data": {
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "title": "Presentation geometry",
        "body": "- Graph extent, the root-to-ground interface frame, Surface bounds, and internal graph camera are distinct values.\n- Node `width` and `height` size the node shell in its owning graph.\n- The authored root-to-ground frame is the graph-backed node's shape in a workspace. Its border, hit area, Minimap window, edge apertures, and semantic-zoom measurement share those bounds.\n- An unfocused graph-backed node clips nodes and edges outside that frame. Authors enlarge or reshape the frame when that material must appear in the node or its Minimap representation.\n- Workspace zoom scales the authored shape and uses its resulting screen occupancy to choose semantic representation.\n- A focused graph unfolds the complete source graph. Camera rollover may then transfer control into graph-local scope; neither operation enlarges the authored workspace shape.\n- The active graph's main minimap is a navigation instrument over the complete graph.\n- A deliberate workspace resize is an arrangement-local viewport override. It does not move source nodes or change graph extent.",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "structural-model"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/templates/page-template/classes/page-section.node-class.node"
      },
      "inputs": [
