    {
      "id": "structural-model-section-5",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Remaining model gaps",
      "position": {
        "x": -180,
        "y": 80
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 320,
      "data": {
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "title": "Remaining model gaps",
        "body": "### P0 — Face fitting and camera rollover\n\nDefine:\n\n- whether a face uses responsive, contain, cover, or fixed-aspect fitting;\n- exact hysteresis and anchor rules when zoom crosses between workspace and graph-local camera scope.\n\n### P0 — Edge lanes\n\nDefine lane identity, ownership, allocation, routing, editing, projection across graph/workspace seams, persistence, and interaction with manual route pins. See [Edge Lane Contract](https://twilite.zone/library/documentation/contracts/edges/edge-lane-contract.md).\n\n### P1 — Current-graph conformance and migration\n\nCreate an executable profile that distinguishes valid current graphs, valid legacy graphs readable through compatibility, incomplete graphs missing required identity or presentation, and mechanical migrations from legacy inline Port presentation and duplicated root Ports.",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "structural-model"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/templates/page-template/classes/page-section.node-class.node"
      },
      "inputs": [
        {
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
